BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:RUSUNUNGUKO (liberty / independence / freedom)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20240411
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270626
DTSTAMP:20260818T112247Z
UID:34603b5d23c7006d137db55ad880@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Designer and visual artist Nontsikelelo Mutiti is the assistan
 t professor and director of graduate studies in graphic design at the Yale
  School of Art. Mutiti’s printed works\, films\, and installations engag
 e with the history and aesthetics of hair braiding in black life. “Ruka
 ” (Shona for “to weave\, braid\, or knit”) brings social binding alo
 ngside physical braiding\; the arrangements of salons\, living rooms\, and
  porches where hair is braided provide social contexts for her projects.\n
 \nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/rusununguko-liberty-independence-free
 dom
LOCATION:The Dome Gallery | Yale Schwarzman Center\, 168 Grove Street\, Ne
 w Haven CT\, 06511
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/rusununguko-liberty-independence-freedom
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Downtown Mystic Ghost Tours
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTSTAMP:20260818T112247Z
UID:84b25dc48e9bfb13f9ce1fcdc754@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Our Original Ghost Walk takes travelers through the historic d
 owntown Mystic landscape crossing the bascule bridge between both sides of
  the Mystic River\, guests will become immersed in the dark\, sordid and s
 upernatural history of New England’s famous seafaring village. From 17th
  century strife of colonial life amidst the Pequot Wars and the King Phill
 ip’s war to mysterious turn of the century murders\, Mystic’s history 
 was founded in darkness. As the centuries grew\, lost seafarers\, creepy c
 ryptids\, and scandalous happenings took place in our quaint seaside commu
 nity.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/downtown-mystic-ghost-tours-1
LOCATION:Liberty Pole Square\, East Main Street\, Holmes Street\, Mystic C
 T\, 06355
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/downtown-mystic-ghost-tours-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paranormal Pub Crawl
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
DTSTAMP:20260818T112247Z
UID:7d76d5286e75cc8458cf866047eb@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join Seaside Shadows for a spirited night out with our Paranor
 mal Pub Crawl—a thrilling “just a beer” ghost tour through Mystic’
 s most haunted and historic taverns! On the second Friday of every month\,
  March through August\, or first Friday of every month\, September through
  December sip and shiver as you enjoy three beers included with your ticke
 t while uncovering eerie tales of the supernatural.\n\nSource: https://ctv
 isit.com/events/paranormal-pub-crawl-1
LOCATION:Bank Square\, Water Street\, West Main Street\, Mystic CT\, 06355
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/paranormal-pub-crawl-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lockwood-Mathews Mansion Museum to open its 2026 Season with a
  new exhibition on Irish American Art with a loan courtesy of Quinnipiac U
 niversity in conjunction with IGHMF
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260312
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTSTAMP:20260818T112247Z
UID:da14d852c63a67abe1d2079c1036@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:With a loan courtesy of Quinnipiac University\, in conjunction
  with Ireland’s Great Hunger Museum of Fairfield\, the Lockwood-Mathews 
 Mansion Museum is currently showing a new exhibition titled\, “A Journey
  of Hope: The Irish American Immigrant Experience.” The exhibit will run
  through Sept. 6\, 2026\, and feature paintings and sculptures displayed i
 n the Mansion’s Art Gallery as well as in the Servants’ Quarters. View
 ing will be included with the purchase of a guided tour.\n\nSource: https:
 //ctvisit.com/events/lockwood-mathews-mansion-museum-open-its-2026-season-
 new-exhibition-irish-american-art-loan
LOCATION:Lockwood Mathews Mansion Museum\, 295 West Avenue\, Norwalk CT\, 
 06850
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/lockwood-mathews-mansion-museum-open-its-20
 26-season-new-exhibition-irish-american-art-loan
